From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:05:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: poll the QDMA in softirq context, one CPU per IRQ bank

The QDMA NAPI leaves thread mode and runs in softirq context, at the
exit of the interrupt. This applies to all RX rings and to the TX
completion NAPIs of both QDMAs. The kernel is built with PREEMPT_NONE
and HZ=100, so a NAPI kernel thread that wakes up waits for a task
that runs in kernel mode on the same CPU, and a 128-entry LRO ring
overflowed in that time while the CPUs had idle time.

Softirq mode alone puts the work of all LRO rings on one CPU: RX
rings 12 to 15 all belonged to IRQ bank 0, and all bank interrupts
start on CPU0. RPS cannot spread that load on the PON path: the skb
reaches the single-queue pon net_device with the ring number as its
RX queue, so get_rps_cpu() does not steer it. Ring 12 stays on bank
0, rings 13, 14 and 15 move to banks 1, 2 and 3, and bank n of each
QDMA gets CPU n as its default affinity. User space can still change
the affinity.

Bank 1 also serves rings 21 to 30, and banks 2 and 3 also serve
rings 5 and 6, so that work moves to CPUs 1 to 3 as well. Bank 0
keeps the TX completions.

irq_set_affinity() is used and not irq_set_affinity_and_hint(),
because a stored hint must be cleared before the devm release of
the interrupt. A failed affinity write is logged, because the bank
then stays on the boot CPU with all the others. The masks get a U
suffix, because INT_RX0_MASK() shifts them left by 16.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c |   12 ++++++++++--
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h |    8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1717,6 +1717,7 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_irq_banks(st
 		struct airoha_irq_bank *irq_bank = &qdma->irq_banks[i];
 		int err, irq_index = 4 * id + i;
 		const char *name;
+		unsigned int cpu;
 
 		spin_lock_init(&irq_bank->irq_lock);
 		irq_bank->qdma = qdma;
@@ -1735,6 +1736,15 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_irq_banks(st
 				       irq_bank);
 		if (err)
 			return err;
+
+		/* The LRO rings are split over the banks, so one CPU per bank
+		 * keeps their softirq work off a single CPU.
+		 */
+		cpu = cpumask_local_spread(i, NUMA_NO_NODE);
+		err = irq_set_affinity(irq_bank->irq, cpumask_of(cpu));
+		if (err)
+			dev_warn(eth->dev, "irq %d stays on the boot CPU: %d\n",
+				 irq_bank->irq, err);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
@@ -4314,8 +4324,6 @@ static int airoha_probe(struct platform_
 	if (!eth->napi_dev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	/* Enable threaded NAPI by default */
-	eth->napi_dev->threaded = true;
 	strscpy(eth->napi_dev->name, "qdma_eth", sizeof(eth->napi_dev->name));
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, eth);
 
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -602,10 +602,10 @@ struct airoha_flow_table_entry {
 };
 
 /* RX queue to IRQ mapping: BIT(q) in IRQ(n) */
-#define RX_IRQ0_BANK_PIN_MASK			0xfb9f
-#define RX_IRQ1_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x7fe00000
-#define RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x20
-#define RX_IRQ3_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x40
+#define RX_IRQ0_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x1b9fU
+#define RX_IRQ1_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x7fe02000U
+#define RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x4020U
+#define RX_IRQ3_BANK_PIN_MASK			0x8040U
 #define RX_IRQ_BANK_PIN_MASK(_n)		\
 	(((_n) == 3) ? RX_IRQ3_BANK_PIN_MASK :	\
 	 ((_n) == 2) ? RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK :	\
